  "decision_needed": [],
  "notes": "Cash basis county. Receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement Total column (p4); Taxes 3,731,421 equals the Statement of Activities Property tax (p2). Beginning cash is not printed (only beginning fund balance 4,063,652); ending cash 4,200,889 from the funds balance statement (p3). Balance sheet from the governmental funds statement of assets and fund balances (totals equal the government-wide statement p1). Detail from each fund's budget-and-actual schedule (pp5-22), which are more detailed than the nonmajor combining schedule (pp23-24), so the combining columns are not recorded again. Lines with a budget but no actual (General Fund federal/nonrevenue, Road and Bridge federal, STOP capital outlay, Inheritance Tax transfers out, Veteran's Aid operating expenses) are omitted; the Drug Enforcement Fund (p14) had no activity. Local receipts lines (context label) are left other per the user ruling 2026-11-12 (FY2023 used charges for services). State receipts left other state aid (no highway allocation printed). Wireless 911 Fund's (24,648) is printed under 'Operating transfers in' (recorded as a negative Transfers In); the combining schedule shows it as transfers out. Highway Bridge Buyback and Road Sinking capital outlay functions follow the budget schedule headings (combining schedule shows different functions). Read pages 1-24 of 24."
}
